# 2026-08-10 20:03:41.176783
+Fix the agent delegation flow according to these requirements:
+
+1. CELEBRITY SIDE (InviteManagerDialog.tsx):
+   - Any user can delegate an agent from Settings without switching account types.
+   - Generate a short, simple link and a 6-digit code.
+   - The share button must use the Web Share API to share the link and code to ANY app (WhatsApp, Telegram, Messages, etc.).
+   - If Web Share API is not available, fall back to copying the link and code to the clipboard with a clear success message.
+   - The sharing process must be extremely smooth and simple: ONE tap to share.
+
+2. AGENT SIDE (RedeemManagerInvite.tsx):
+   - The agent opens the shared link. The code should be pre-filled from the URL if possible.
+   - If manual code entry is required, the input field MUST be LTR (left-to-right) to prevent code reversal in RTL interface.
+   - The agent simply enters the code (or it's auto-filled) and taps ONE button to accept and become the manager.
+   - The process must be extremely simple: open link → see code → tap "Accept" → done.
+
+3. GENERAL:
+   - The entire flow (celebrity generates link → shares → agent opens → accepts) must be smooth and seamless.
+   - No complicated steps. No confusing UI. No code reversal issues.
+
+Update InviteManagerDialog.tsx, RedeemManagerInvite.tsx, and useRole.tsx as needed.

